name deny-release-broken-1
timeout 280

# `objective deny release` UNMET — the kill succeeded and the mission still failed (round C12).
# Byte-identical to deny-release.fbm except for ONE number: the striker's briefed pickle is at t=15
# instead of t=90, i.e. 55 s before the round that kills it arrives.
#
# READING RULE (binding): TIMEOUT/exit 3 is the pass criterion, and the defender's RESULT reason must be
# "sim time exceeded the mission timeout" — an unmet objective at the end of the run, not a FAIL, because
# nothing in `deny release` can be VIOLATED in a way that decides a run early (there is no tick at which
# "he will never release" becomes false; only the end of the run answers it). `events.log` must contain
# `sms RELEASE unit=striker` and the run must still not exit 0. An exit 0 here would mean the denial was
# scored from the kill, which is precisely the conflation this objective exists to prevent.
#
# THE CHAIN, MEASURED: the striker pickles at t=15.6 (Mk-82, station 3) and that store impacts the ground
# at t=59.1. The defender's own first round is away at t=20.4 and its second kills the striker at t=70.5
# (miss distance 4.80 m). So the KILL objective is met, `survive` is met, and the run is still not a
# success: the ordnance was already off the rails 55 s before the raider died. That is the entire value
# of the kind, stated as a measurement.

unit defender
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.60000 8000 90.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 20                     # ~22 nm head-on: inside the launch zone
  wp 46.90000 7.15000 8000 400
  objective kill unit striker
  objective deny release unit striker
  objective survive

unit striker
  team hostile
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 7.30000 8000 270.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 15                     # <<< THE ONE NUMBER that differs from deny-release
  wp 46.90000 6.75000 8000 400
